      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "AIM",
          "content": "To report about an additional case of biliary ileus after bariatric surgery is reported and extensively reviewing the literature on this topic."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "MATERIAL OF STUDY",
          "content": "We reviewed the literature and found three cases of gallstone ileus (GI) that occurred after bariatric surgery."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "DISCUSSION",
          "content": "A 41 year old patient presented a GI eight years after a biliointestinal bypass (BIB) for morbid obesity. The patient complained of abdominal pain for two weeks. Computed tomography (CT) and abdominal ultrasound (US) allowed a preoperative diagnosis of GI and planning of surgical strategy. Surgical treatment was carried out through laparoscopic-assisted enterolithotomy alone procedure. This choice is supported discussing the related issues: morbidity, potential recurrence, eventual developing of gallbladder carcinoma."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "It is the first reported case of GI after BIB preoperatively diagnosed through CT scan and US, and treated with a laparoscopic assisted approach. Additional considerations concerning preoperative diagnosis, surgical strategy, technical details and follow-up can be usefully applied even in non post-bariatric biliary ileus."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "KEY WORDS",
          "content": "Biliointestinal bypass, Gallstone ileus, Laparoscopy, Ultrasonography."
        }
      ]},
